<title>ISRAEL: TENNIS-ISRAEL OPEN RESULTS.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-ISRAEL OPEN RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>First round results on the</p>
<p>opening day of the $328,000 Israel Open tennis tournament on</p>
<p>Monday (prefix number denotes seeding):</p>
<p>1-MaliVai Washington (U.S.) beat Stephane Simian (France) 6-1</p>
<p>6-4</p>
<p>Martin Sinner (Germany) beat Noam Behr (Israel) 6-4 6-3</p>
<p>Gustavo Kuerten (Brazil) beat David Nainkin (South Africa) 6-3</p>
<p>7-5</p>
<p>Sargis Sargsian (Armenia) beat Justin Gimelstob (U.S.) 6-3 6-1</p>
<p>5-Hernan Gumy (Argentina) beat Luis Adrian Morejon (Ecuador)</p>
<p>6-3 6-3</p>
<p>Marcos Ondruska (South Africa) beat Michael Tebbutt (Australia)</p>
<p>3-6 7-6 (7-2) 7-6 (7-1)</p>
<p>Nicolas Pereira (Venezuela) beat Marcos Aurelio Gorriz (Spain)</p>
<p>6-2 6-3</p>
<p>Johan van Herck (Belgium) beat Oleg Ogorodov (Uzbekistan) 6-4</p>
<p>6-4.</p>
</text>
